            value: "defensive",
          },
          {
            tag: "set_variable",
            name: "ai_directives",
            value: "goal,,,0,20,%7B%22id%22%3A%5B%22Earl%20Lanbec'h%22%5D%7D;goal,,,0,10,%7B%22id%22%3A%5B%22Kapou'e%22%5D%7D;goal,,,0,20,%7B%22id%22%3A%5B%22Howgarth%20III%22%5D%7D",
          },
        ],
      },
      {
        tag: "event",
        id: "story_25",
        on: "start",
        children: [
          {
            tag: "message",
            speaker: "narrator",
            text: _("Kapou’e agreed to meet Howgarth III. Not trusting the human however, Kapou’e brought along Grüü, as well as one of his most trusted soldiers. Earl Lanbec’h flatly refused to attend the parley."),
          },
        ],
      },
      {
        tag: "event",
        id: "story_26",
        on: "start",
        children: [
          {
            tag: "message",
            speaker: "narrator",
            text: _("The human attack having stopped for the time being, both parties met in the middle of the battlefield. Howgarth III demanded that Kapou’e give Dorest back to the humans and return to their lands as defined in the treaty. Kapou’e refused to do so as long as the humans were attacking orcish lands. He demanded that the humans disperse their forces and return any land they had stolen from the orcs. Only then would he return Dorest and disperse the Horde."),
          },
        ],
      },
      {
        tag: "event",
        id: "story_27",
        on: "start",
        children: [
          {
            tag: "message",
            speaker: "narrator",
            text: _("Howgarth III agreed and further added that, if Earl Lanbec’h continued in aggression, then under the dictates of the Northern Alliance, he himself would be forced to move against the Earl."),
          },
        ],
      },
      {
        tag: "event",
        id: "story_28",
        on: "start",
        children: [
          {
            tag: "message",
            speaker: "narrator",
            text: _("That having been settled, Kapou’e began to inquire about the death of his father. Howgarth III repeated his story, that the last thing they heard from Black-Eye Karun was the message declining their invitation to join the Northern Alliance, brought by none other than Shan Taum himself."),
          },
        ],
      },
      {
        tag: "event",
        id: "story_29",
        on: "start",
        children: [
          {
            tag: "message",
            speaker: "narrator",
            text: _("As they were discussing the matter, a group of orcs charged from the surrounding trees and hills and surrounded the parley."),
          },
        ],
      },
      {
        tag: "event",
        id: "loyal_30",
